    {
      "@id": "q1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "What new statistical methods can be developed to detect problematic data based on summary results alone"
    },
    {
      "@id": "q2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "what is the estimated prevalence of potentially problematic data in the ClinicalTrials.gov database?"
    },
    {
      "@id": "q3-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "do the prevalence estimates of potentially problematic data in the ClinicalTrials.gov database show a change over time?"
    },
    {
      "@id": "q4-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "are prevalence estimates of potentially problematic data in the ClinicalTrials.gov database predicted by study characteristics"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "If the clinical trial data are problematic, these decisions are undermined."
    },
    {
      "@id": "c2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "this remains a niche field despite the large scientific and societal benefits of improving these methods"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c3-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "It remains unclear how prevalent problematic data is throughout the different sciences"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c3-quote-1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "systematic data on how prevalent problematic data are and how the prevalence has developed over time are largely absent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c4-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "it is plausible that it underestimates the true extent of the problem due to response bias"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c5-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "systematic application of these methods would provide a prevalence estimate of problematic data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c6-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "the principle of stochasticity can be applied to help detect potentially problematic data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c7-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "problematic data by one location might be masked by aggregating and consequently remain undetected"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c8-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "the probability of a positive result due to sample fluctuations (i.e., false positive) decreases"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c9-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "the hypothesis that industry-funded research is more frequently problematic than publicly funded research"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c10-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "These detection tools might also serve as a deterrent for data fabrication"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c12-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "a new way to estimate the prevalence of problematic data, moving away from biased self-reports"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c14-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "The CT database, where information on clinical trials are available from beginning to completion, allows for a substantial amount of meta-research"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c15-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "it might appear that more problematic data are published now than a decade ago"
    },
    {
      "@id": "c16-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "the statistical detection tools would be of interest to the Office of Research Integrity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "indicated beta-blockers actually increased perioperative mortality if the results of the problematic studies were excluded"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Approximately 2% of all researchers admit to having fabricated data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev3-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "was present in 1% of their accepted manuscripts"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev4-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "168 trials by Fuji were analyzed based on published summary results"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev4-quote-1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "subsequently resulted in more than 100 retractions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev5-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "the Fuji case in anesthesiology"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev6-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "but none of these publications explicitly inspected potentially problematic data"
    },
    {
      "@id": "ev7-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "which includes over 100,000 completed trials with summary results for more than 15,000 clinical trials"
    },
    {
      "@id": "s1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "This project aims to develop new methods and apply them to results reported in the ClinicalTrials.gov database."
    },
    {
      "@id": "s1-quote-1",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Table 1 includes a preliminary specification of activities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "s2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "These methods would be tested in simulation studies for their validity before applying them to the CT data themselves."
    },
    {
      "@id": "s3-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "the Smeesters case, and the Sanna case in psychology (Simonsohn 2013)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "s4-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "which indicated that these trials were problematic (Carlisle 2012, Carlisle et al. 2015)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "s5-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "A subsequent meta-analysis"
    },
    {
      "@id": "p1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "examines the “variance of variances.”"
    },
    {
      "@id": "p2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "an overall χ2-test for potentially problematic data in the baseline is computed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "p3-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "The data from the CT database will be extracted and structured prior to the start of the project."
    },
    {
      "@id": "r1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "will be implemented into the `ddfab` package in R"
    },
    {
      "@id": "r2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "will be checked by another researcher (i.e., co-piloted)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sd1-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Just post it: The lesson from two cases of fabricated data detected by statistics alone"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sd2-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "The analysis of 168 randomised controlled trials to test data integrity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sd3-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Meta-analysis of secure randomised controlled trials of β-blockade to prevent perioperative death"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sd4-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "How many scientists fabricate and falsify research?"
    },
    {
      "@id": "e7-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "As a result, patients were exposed to increased risk instead of decreased risk"
    },
    {
      "@id": "e8-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "Since the 2% estimate is based on self-reports"
    },
    {
      "@id": "e12-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "used statistical tools to indicate that results were too good to be true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "e22-quote-0",
      "@type": "Item",
      "content": "However, systematic data on how prevalent problematic data are and how the prevalence has developed over time are largely absent"
    }
  ]
}